// Title: Windows Kernel Debugger Execution
// Sigma ID: 27ee9438-90dc-4bef-904b-d3ef927f5e7e
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-05-15 | Modified: 2024-04-24
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, stealth
// Description: Detects execution of the Windows Kernel Debugger "kd.exe".
// False positives:
//   - Rare occasions of legitimate cases where kernel debugging is necessary in production. Investigation is required
// References:
//   - Internal Research
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_kd_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\kd.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "kd.exe"
